prompt:
the most important historical Jewish events that happened in the world, dates to the left of them
$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$
| Date                 | Historical Jewish Event                                                                           |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **c. 1800–1700 BCE** | Traditional era associated with Abraham, regarded as the founding patriarch of the Jewish people. |
| **c. 1250 BCE**      | Traditional date of the Exodus from Egypt under Moses.                                            |
| **c. 1000 BCE**      | David establishes Jerusalem as the capital of ancient Israel.                                     |
| **c. 960 BCE**       | Construction of the First Temple by Solomon.                                                      |
| **586 BCE**          | Babylonian Destruction of the First Temple and the Babylonian Exile.                              |
| **516 BCE**          | Completion of the Second Temple in Jerusalem.                                                     |
| **167–160 BCE**      | Maccabean Revolt; foundation of the Hanukkah story.                                               |
| **70 CE**            | Roman Destruction of the Second Temple, a turning point in Jewish history.                        |
| **132–136 CE**       | Bar Kokhba Revolt ends with massive loss of life and dispersion.                                  |
| **1096**             | Massacres of Jewish communities during the First Crusade.                                         |
| **1492**             | Alhambra Decree forces Jews to leave Spain.                                                       |
| **1897**             | Theodor Herzl convenes the First Zionist Congress.                                                |
| **1917**             | Balfour Declaration supports the establishment of a Jewish national home in Palestine.            |
| **1933**             | Adolf Hitler comes to power in Germany, beginning systematic persecution of Jews.                 |
| **1939–1945**        | Holocaust; approximately six million Jews are murdered by Nazi Germany and its collaborators.     |
| **May 14, 1948**     | Israeli Declaration of Independence establishes the modern State of Israel.                       |
| **1961**             | Trial of Adolf Eichmann in Jerusalem brings extensive public attention to Holocaust testimony.    |
| **1967**             | Six-Day War significantly reshapes the Middle East and Jewish history.                            |
| **1973**             | Yom Kippur War.                                                                                   |
| **2023**             | October 7 attacks and the ensuing war become a major event in contemporary Jewish history.        |
